> ## Documentation Index
> Fetch the complete documentation index at: https://docs.crustdata.com/llms.txt
> Use this file to discover all available pages before exploring further.
# Person Search
> Find people with the Person Search API, from a simple name lookup to a query with many filters.
Use the Person Search API to find people by name, title, company, location, and other fields. This page shows:
* Your first search.
* The shape of the response.
* How to combine filters.
* Example requests and recipes that you can copy and change.
For the operator list, the field catalog, and the validation rules, see [Search reference](/person-docs/search/reference).
Send every request to this endpoint:
```
POST https://api.crustdata.com/person/search
```
<Note>
  In each example, replace `REDACTED` with your API key. Every request
  must include the `x-api-version: 2025-11-01` header.
</Note>
<Callout icon="coins" color="#5345e4">
  <strong>Pricing:</strong> The base price is <code>0.03 credits per
  result</code>. Each premium group that you filter on or receive adds a
  per-result charge:
  * Experience, education, and skills: <code>0.1</code>.
  * Certifications, honors, professional network signals, languages, and
    summary: <code>0.2</code>.
  * Dev platform profile filters: <code>0.8</code> (profile) or
    <code>2.5</code> (repositories).
  * Research profiles (enabled on request): <code>0.4</code>.
  A filter on a premium group is one charge. The same group in the response
  is a separate charge. Sorting is free. A request with no
  <code>fields</code> returns experience and education, so it costs
  <code>0.23</code> per result on the standard plan. For the full table, see
  [Premium fields in search](/general/pricing#premium-fields-in-search). For
  your own prices, open the [**Pricing** tab](https://app.crustdata.com/endpoints/person-search#pricing) in the
  dashboard or call [`/account/endpoints`](/general/permissions).
</Callout>
<Tip>
  For the full table of `filters.field` values that you can filter on, see
  [Searchable fields](/person-docs/search/reference#searchable-fields) in the
  search reference. The table groups the fields by family. The reference
  also shows a one-line way to get the live list from the API.
</Tip>
<CardGroup cols={3}>
  <Card title="Examples" icon="list-filter" href="#example-requests">
    See requests for employer and title, geo radius, country, and post-processing exclusions.
  </Card>
  <Card title="Pagination and sorting" icon="list-ordered" href="/person-docs/search/reference#paginate-through-results">
